<h2>Sound in air</h2>

<p>At about <tex>343\ \mathrm{m/s}</tex>, doubling the frequency halves the wavelength:</p>

<chart type=line title="Wavelength (m) of sound at frequency f" width=95%>
  frequency, wavelength
  100 Hz, 3.43
  200 Hz, 1.72
  400 Hz, 0.86
  800 Hz, 0.43
  1600 Hz, 0.21
</chart>
